IMPORT prelude

-- Human Cloning and Other Prohibited Practices Act 2004 (Singapore) -- what counts as a human embryo, a clone and a prohibited
-- embryo (s 2), the prohibited practices (ss 5 to 13, including the ban on paying for eggs, sperm and embryos), the enforcement
-- offences and retention of seized articles (ss 14(3), (4), (6), 16), liability of officers and partners (s 17) and the penalties
-- (s 18).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/5/2023", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HCOPPA2004.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 11 of 2023 wef 01/05/2023 (the Director-General of Health takes over administration).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0026 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. For an ordinary person or a fertility clinic the Act meets them at IVF, donation of eggs or sperm, and payment for
-- them. Not encoded: administration and appointment of enforcement officers (s 4), the powers of entry, search and seizure
-- themselves (s 14(1), (2), (5)), protection from personal liability (s 15), the Public Prosecutor's consent to prosecute
-- (s 19, quoted only), District Court jurisdiction (s 20), service of documents (s 21) and regulations (s 22). No regulation prescribing "such other thing" as a prohibited embryo (s 2(1)
-- "prohibited embryo" (c)) was retrieved; it is a flag here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Cloning and Other Prohibited Practices Act 2004 -- prohibited practices`

§§ `2 -- human embryo, human embryo clone, prohibited embryo`

-- s 2(1): "human embryo" means any live embryo that "(a) has a human genome or an altered human genome; and (b) has been
-- developing for less than 8 weeks since the appearance of 2 pro-nuclei or the initiation of its development by other means";
-- (3): "any period when the development of the embryo is suspended is to be disregarded". 8 weeks is taken as 56 days.
-- "human embryo clone" means any human embryo "that is a genetic copy of another living or dead human, but does not include a human
-- embryo created by the fertilisation of a human egg by human sperm"; (2) the copy need not be identical; (4) an embryo from
-- "embryo splitting is not to be taken as created by a process of fertilisation".
-- "prohibited embryo" means "(a) any human embryo that has been developing outside the body of a woman for a period of more than
-- 14 days, excluding any period when the development is suspended; (b) any human embryo that was removed from the body of a woman
-- by a person intending to collect a viable human embryo; or (c) such other thing as may be prescribed".
DECLARE Embryo HAS
    `is live` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a human or altered human genome` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an animal embryo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of development, excluding suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `days developing outside the body of a woman, excluding suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `created by fertilisation of a human egg by human sperm (not embryo splitting)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a genetic copy of another living or dead human` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was removed from a woman by a person intending to collect a viable embryo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is prescribed to be a prohibited embryo` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a human embryo` IF
        `the embryo`'s `is live`
    AND `the embryo`'s `has a human or altered human genome`
    AND `the embryo`'s `days of development, excluding suspension` LESS THAN 56

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a human embryo clone` IF
        `is a human embryo` `the embryo`
    AND `the embryo`'s `is a genetic copy of another living or dead human`
    AND (NOT `the embryo`'s `created by fertilisation of a human egg by human sperm (not embryo splitting)`)

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prohibited embryo` IF
        `the embryo`'s `is prescribed to be a prohibited embryo`
    OR  (    `is a human embryo` `the embryo`
         AND (    `the embryo`'s `days developing outside the body of a woman, excluding suspension` GREATER THAN 14
              OR  `the embryo`'s `was removed from a woman by a person intending to collect a viable embryo`))

§§ `5, 6 -- human cloning`

-- s 5: "A person must not place any human embryo clone in the body of a human or the body of an animal."
-- s 6: "It is not a defence to an offence under section 5 that the human embryo clone did not survive or could not have survived."
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `a woman's reproductive tract`
    `a woman's body outside the reproductive tract`
    `a man's body`
    `an animal's body`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the body of a human` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `an animal's body` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the body of a woman` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `a woman's reproductive tract` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a woman's body outside the reproductive tract` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- `the clone survived or could have survived` is taken and deliberately ignored: s 6.
GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo, `the place` IS A Place, `the clone survived or could have survived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `placing it contravenes section 5` IF
    `is a human embryo clone` `the embryo`

§§ `7, 8, 9 -- development beyond 14 days and collection`

-- s 7: "A person must not develop any human embryo, that is created by a process other than the fertilisation of a human egg by
-- human sperm, for a period of more than 14 days, excluding any period when the development of the embryo is suspended."
-- s 8: "A person must not develop any human embryo outside the body of a woman for a period of more than 14 days" (same exclusion).
-- s 9: "A person must not remove any human embryo from the body of a woman for the purpose of collecting a viable human embryo."
-- The embryo's own days of development stand in for the period of the person's developing it (an inference).
GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `developing it contravenes section 7` IF
        `is a human embryo` `the embryo`
    AND (NOT `the embryo`'s `created by fertilisation of a human egg by human sperm (not embryo splitting)`)
    AND `the embryo`'s `days of development, excluding suspension` GREATER THAN 14

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `developing it contravenes section 8` IF
        `is a human embryo` `the embryo`
    AND `the embryo`'s `days developing outside the body of a woman, excluding suspension` GREATER THAN 14

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removing it contravenes section 9` IF
        `is a human embryo` `the embryo`
    AND `the embryo`'s `was removed from a woman by a person intending to collect a viable embryo`

§§ `10, 11 -- where an embryo may be placed`

-- s 10: a person must not "(a) place any human embryo in an animal; (b) place any human embryo in the body of a human, other than
-- in a woman's reproductive tract; or (c) place any animal embryo in the body of a human for any period of gestation".
-- s 11: "A person must not place any embryo in the body of a woman knowing that, or reckless as to whether, the embryo is a
-- prohibited embryo."
GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo, `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `placing it contravenes section 10` IF
        (    `is a human embryo` `the embryo`
         AND (NOT (`the place` EQUALS `a woman's reproductive tract`)))
    OR  (`the embryo`'s `is an animal embryo` AND `is the body of a human` `the place`)

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo, `the place` IS A Place, `knew or was reckless that it was prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `placing it contravenes section 11` IF
        `is the body of a woman` `the place`
    AND `is a prohibited embryo` `the embryo`
    AND `knew or was reckless that it was prohibited`

GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo, `the place` IS A Place, `the clone survived or could have survived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or was reckless that it was prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `placing it is a prohibited practice` IF
        `placing it contravenes section 5` `the embryo` `the place` `the clone survived or could have survived`
    OR  `placing it contravenes section 10` `the embryo` `the place`
    OR  `placing it contravenes section 11` `the embryo` `the place` `knew or was reckless that it was prohibited`

§§ `12 -- import and export`

-- s 12: "A person must not knowingly -- (a) import any prohibited embryo into Singapore; or (b) export any prohibited embryo out of
-- Singapore."
GIVEN `the embryo` IS AN Embryo, `imported or exported` IS A BOOLEAN, `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `moving it across the border contravenes section 12` IF
    `imported or exported` AND `knowingly` AND `is a prohibited embryo` `the embryo`

§§ `13 -- no trade in eggs, sperm and embryos`

-- s 13(1): a person must not "(a) give or offer valuable consideration to another person; or (b) receive, or offer to receive,
-- valuable consideration from another person, for the supply of any human egg, human sperm or human embryo".
-- (2): a contract or arrangement in contravention "is void"; (3) not one "providing only for the reimbursement of any reasonable
-- expenses". (4): "supply" does not include "the provision of any service for facilitating the donation and receipt" by
-- "receiving, storing, processing and subsequently implanting" donated material, "whether or not for consideration".
-- (5): "valuable consideration" "includes any inducement, discount or priority in the provision of a service to the person, but
-- does not include the payment of reasonable expenses"; reasonable expenses include collection, storage or transport (for an
-- embryo, storage or transport).
-- Treating the part of a payment above reasonable expenses as valuable consideration is an inference: the text excludes only
-- "the payment of reasonable expenses".
DECLARE Dealing HAS
    `concerns a human egg, human sperm or human embryo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is only a service of receiving, storing, processing and implanting donated material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `money given, offered or asked for` IS A NUMBER
    `reasonable expenses incurred in the supply` IS A NUMBER
    `an inducement, discount or priority in a service is given or offered` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is valuable consideration` IF
        `the dealing`'s `money given, offered or asked for` GREATER THAN `the dealing`'s `reasonable expenses incurred in the supply`
    OR  `the dealing`'s `an inducement, discount or priority in a service is given or offered`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing contravenes section 13(1)` IF
        `the dealing`'s `concerns a human egg, human sperm or human embryo`
    AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `is only a service of receiving, storing, processing and implanting donated material`)
    AND `there is valuable consideration` `the dealing`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is void under section 13(2)` IF
    `the dealing contravenes section 13(1)` `the dealing`

§§ `14(3), (4) -- how long a seized article may be kept`

-- s 14(3): an article seized "may be retained by the Director-General for a period of 6 months or such longer period as a
-- Magistrate's Court may, on application by an enforcement officer, allow". (4): if within that period proceedings are commenced
-- and the article is relevant, it may be retained "until the conclusion of those proceedings".
GIVEN `months since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `further months allowed by a Magistrate's Court` IS A NUMBER,
      `relevant proceedings commenced within the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `those proceedings have concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may retain the article` IF
        `months since seizure` AT MOST (6 + `further months allowed by a Magistrate's Court`)
    OR  (`relevant proceedings commenced within the period` AND (NOT `those proceedings have concluded`))

§§ `14(6), 16, 18 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 14(6): "(a) without reasonable excuse, refuses or fails to comply with any requirement of an enforcement officer" or "(b) gives
-- any false or misleading information" -- fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
-- s 16: obstructing, hindering or impeding an enforcement officer -- the same.
-- s 18: contravening "section 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 or 13(1)" -- fine not exceeding $100,000 or imprisonment not exceeding
-- 10 years or both.
GIVEN `failed to comply with a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-compliance is an offence under section 14(6)(a)` IF
    `failed to comply with a requirement` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `a prohibited practice under section 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 or 13(1)`
    `failing to comply with an enforcement officer's requirement`
    `giving an enforcement officer false or misleading information`
    `obstructing an enforcement officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a prohibited practice under section 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 or 13(1)` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a prohibited practice under section 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 or 13(1)` THEN 120
    OTHERWISE 12

§§ `17, 19 -- who is liable, and who may prosecute`

-- s 17(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer
-- of the body corporate; or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer's part, the officer as well as the body corporate
-- shall be guilty"; (3), (4) the same for partners and for officers or governing-body members of an unincorporated association.
-- (5): "officer" includes a director, manager, secretary "and includes any person purporting to act in any such capacity".
-- s 19: "No prosecution ... may be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor." (Noted, not encoded.)
GIVEN `the organisation committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an officer or partner of it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the offence is attributable to their neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer or partner is also guilty under section 17` IF
        `the organisation committed an offence under the Act`
    AND `is an officer or partner of it`
    AND (`consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to their neglect`)

